<title>MEXICO: Tribasa wins Mexican contracts worth 76 mln pesos.</title>
<headline>Tribasa wins Mexican contracts worth 76 mln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction firm Grupo Tribasa SA de CV said Thursday that it recently has won several contracts worth a total of 76 million pesos.</p>
<p>Tribasa will be able to complete all the jobs without borrowing any money, company spokesman Jorge Coo told Reuters.</p>
<p>One contract is worth 37 million pesos for work on the new B line of the Mexico City subway system. In addition, the Communications and Transport Ministry has awarded Tribasa a 19 million peso contract for work on two federal highways. Also, the government of Veracruz state granted Tribasa a 14 million peso contract to build a dam.</p>
<p>Tribasa also won a series of smaller contracts worth six million pesos, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau, +528 345-7617))</p>
